### Time and Language — Reference APIs (PR1: read-only master data)

# FusionX parity: RegionAndLocationMaster (Identifier L=location, R=region/language) and ddlTimeZone options
# from UCWindowsDateTimeSettings.ascx. World / id 39070 excluded from locations. Apply APIs (date/time,
# region, regional format) are PR2–PR4 — not available in PR1.

### Time and Language — Get locations (Identifier = L)
# @name timeLangGetLocations
GET {{Intellinode.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/admin/device-config/time-and-language/reference/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

# Expected: 200 success=true; data[] with id, identifier=L, value (geo location name); excludes World/39070


### Time and Language — Get regions / languages (Identifier = R)
# @name timeLangGetRegions
GET {{Intellinode.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/admin/device-config/time-and-language/reference/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

# Expected: 200 success=true; data[] with id, identifier=R, value, bcp47Code (e.g. en-US, hi-IN)


### Time and Language — Get Windows time zones
# @name timeLangGetTimeZones
GET {{Intellinode.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/admin/device-config/time-and-language/reference/time-zones
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

# Expected: 200 success=true; data[] with id, displayName, windowsTzKey (FusionX ddlTimeZone class / MUI_Display)


### Time and Language — Include inactive master rows (optional query)
GET {{Intellinode.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/admin/device-config/time-and-language/reference/locations?includeInactive=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

# Expected: 200; includes rows where is_active=false when seeded


### Windows Date & Time Setup APIs (Windows :XP only, v1)

# FusionX: System Settings → Time and Language → Date & Time (DateTime / TimeZone / TimeServerSynchro tabs).
# Inline JSON in functionParameter (WinCELinux.XPDATE_TIME) — no hydration. One module_name per applyMode:
#   ManualDateTime → DateTime (signal suffix DT)
#   TimeZone       → TimeZone (signal suffix TZ)
#   TimeServer     → TimeServerSynchro (signal suffix TS)
# Pending task for the SAME module_name blocks a new apply (409 ApplyBlocked); different tabs do not block each other.
# TimeZone apply validates timeZoneDisplay + windowsTzKey against GET .../time-and-language/reference/time-zones.

@dateTimeMac = 00-11-22-33-44-55:XP

### Windows Date & Time — Get current by MAC
# @name dateTimeGetCurrent
GET {{Intellinode.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/admin/device-config/windows-date-time/{{dateTimeMac}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

# Expected: 200 with data.settings.applyMode, settingsVersion, lastApplyStatus


### Windows Date & Time — Execute now (ManualDateTime)
